1635:  Mechanism (mvp.4): each changed tick appends one pointer-only observation row to the Run's own <git-common-dir>/bp3/run-lifecycle-derivations/<run-id>.jsonl (keyed by run-id; session-id is only an InitRecord field) and refreshes its disposable <run-id>.json cache. Since mvp.5 the derivation logs are the sole lifecycle read path; the retired shared maps are never read or written. Writer discipline (followup.1): each row is a single write() on an O_APPEND descriptor and the cache is a uniquely named temp file in the same directory, fsynced and renamed over the old cache, so parallel supervisors never tear a row or the cache; a torn final line is ignored by the fold and reported as W_TORN_TAIL.\n\
1639:  bp3 harness init-check [--engine muse-code|pi]\n\
1671:  Appends the first derivation row (kind init_record) to <git-common-dir>/bp3/run-lifecycle-derivations/<run-id>.jsonl before the child starts, so find-tape/watch/supervisor resolve the Run from birth. Create-only: an existing log for the run-id is E_EXISTS; a bad run-id, engine, or pid is E_USAGE. Emits {ok, run_id, harness, session_id, pid, tape_path, quest, exp, path}.\n\
1676:let help_backtest = "bp3 harness backtest - replay the muse fold over stored tapes (findings, not a gate):\n\
1677:  bp3 harness backtest [--corpus <dir>]\n\
1678:  Reads every .jsonl tape under the corpus (default: the muse tape source), folds mechanical facts per tape (BP3_RUN_ID bindings, bp3 invocations, E_* refusals, commit shas, finish/exit evidence, torn tails) and emits one verdict {ok, engine, corpus, tapes_replayed, identifiable, traces, findings}. Each finding names its tape, run-id, evidence lines, and proposed fix target (bp3 q u, hooks, or adapter). A parser crash fails the call; findings themselves never gate. Truncated, foreign, and torn tapes are reported in findings, never fatal.\n\
1679:Example: bp3 harness backtest --corpus ~/.local/share/muse/sessions\n"
1682:  | "b" | "backtest" -> "backtest"
1692:  | [] -> usage "harness needs a verb: supervisor, init-check, find-tape, watch, desk, record-init, or backtest"
1702:        | "backtest" -> help_backtest
1714:       | "backtest" -> do_backtest rest
